{"title":"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In acute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is the orthocenter, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the centroid, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. It is obvious that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f240f06450bc379ecfbf624a12a7b43be1206153.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM \\ge GM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2fe8c42e41c03c98a7c213c435a311dea0cca30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM \\ge HM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" /> does not always hold. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/337b833c3807f72484c4bccc00ee24bbfd0be814.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC] = 162$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11ed1469a9f377b72a3ba727f83a96599f866c2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, then the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/4/5e46a5d559ffff94b22f2df24968accfa7438cbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> which produces the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2fe8c42e41c03c98a7c213c435a311dea0cca30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM \\ge HM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/560d59a8b28eefaa0b822421f1a78e64d155c1c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b\\sqrt{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> squarefree. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e8f8e7e8de28c78e9d82ab4d31901b41ca9aa25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle ABC] = 168$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11ed1469a9f377b72a3ba727f83a96599f866c2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, we know that the height from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, because the perpendicular is the shortest segment from a line to a point not on the line, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/d/edda30a879cd36ab83138338ba5702b2cda28aa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB \\geq 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"17\" />. Thus, the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/e/73e19ff964c3be3f9ea907ad21466c0a84f29fca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB} \\perp \\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />. This is technically not possible, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is acute, but it may be helpful in getting a better sense of the problem. This scenario is shown below:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/1/001fcbc100482eedd5d87d36cc98676bd9ee1952.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  import geometry;  point A = origin;  point B = (0,18); point C = (18,18); triangle t = triangle(A,B,C);  point M = midpoint(B--C);  circle c = circumcircle(t); point O = circumcenter(t);  point G = centroid(t);  // Triangle and Circumcircle draw(t); draw(c);  // Median AM draw(A--M);  // Labelling Points dot(A); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,SW); dot(B); label(&quot;H=B&quot;,B,NW); dot(C); label(&quot;C&quot;,C,NE); dot(O); label(&quot;O&quot;,O,SE); dot(M); label(&quot;M&quot;,M,N); dot(G); label(&quot;G&quot;,G,WSW);  // Length Labels label(&quot;$9$&quot;,midpoint(B--M),N); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,midpoint(M--C),N); label(&quot;$18$&quot;,midpoint(A--B),W);  // Right Angle Mark markscalefactor = 0.18; draw(rightanglemark(A,B,C));  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"235\" />\n</p><p>Because the orthocenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bd74578f991d04fa47f13139658370a8173772c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HM=BM=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"130\" height=\"14\" />. Now, by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac545ccdb722dca8a6a3081894a957004a9808d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM=9\\sqrt5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"21\" />. Because the centrod is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d98502509e862e72c463b55a42b95925ba25f1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"9\" height=\"21\" /> of the way along the median from the vertex, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/6/8c6fb2df68f555c308f344b264f88fe00395ab43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM=\\tfrac{9\\sqrt5}3=3\\sqrt5&lt;9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"179\" height=\"26\" />. Thus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/1/071777de2749e27ec1a12fc6b48c930c836621a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM&lt;HM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />, so the given inequality does not hold. Now, let us look at the example where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is collinear with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/3/f73bf0b21b1bb1668a9cec8fccbaee4f76502d1d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  import geometry;  point A = origin;  point B = (-9,18); point C = (9,18); triangle t = triangle(A,B,C);  point M = midpoint(B--C);  circle c = circumcircle(t); point O = circumcenter(t);  point G = centroid(t); point H = orthocentercenter(t);  point Cp;  // Triangle and Circumcircle draw(t); draw(c);  // Median AM, Segment OB draw(A--M); draw(O--B);  // Defining C&#39; pair[] cp = intersectionpoints(line(O,C),c); Cp = cp[0];  // Labelling Points dot(A); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,S); dot(B); label(&quot;B&quot;,B,NW); dot(C); label(&quot;C&quot;,C,NE); dot(O); label(&quot;O&quot;,O,SW); dot(M); label(&quot;M&quot;,M,N); dot(G); label(&quot;G&quot;,G,E); dot(H); label(&quot;H&quot;,H,ENE); dot(Cp); label(&quot;C$^{\\prime}$&quot;,Cp,SW);  // Length Labels label(&quot;$9$&quot;,midpoint(B--M),N); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,midpoint(M--C),N);  // Right Angle Mark markscalefactor = 0.18; draw(rightanglemark(A,M,B));  [/asy]\" width=\"232\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>By centroid properties, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84f24796f3bd63291bfc345a48643655bae2cef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG=\\tfrac23 AM = \\tfrac23 \\cdot 18 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"206\" height=\"23\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumradius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Then, by Pythagoras in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/6/2b6e71b19de729f36f4554787c249e178ae642f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OBM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba72206ffb0d19fbd1db2f473cdc06d6b3eacf23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM=\\sqrt{R^2-81}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"21\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0d3d9f5c28a2057ef957e852d23147778101703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA=R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"68\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8febcdef5c7971c2c7c23369b794dc2dd2917aa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" />, we have the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee1a602c4eeb8c693ee08057800e1ab571667d86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{R^2-81}+R=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"157\" height=\"21\" />, which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/9/07936b51b08bb754be9b34b70160d7a93f75e374.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO=R=\\tfrac{45}4&lt;12=AG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"204\" height=\"23\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is acute, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is in the interior of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. This fact, combined with the properties of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euler_Line\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Euler Line\">Euler Line</a>, show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> must be closer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/3/5f3b51e60c99f92d1540c056039c2bc77c45f78c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM&gt;HM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />, and the inequality is thereby satisfied.\n</p><p>As in the above diagram, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/8719862f13b63f924f182b682c6615733f3871f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C^{\\prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> be the point on the circle such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/e/d1ec033ed5c50b061a428f3a54618524c21304df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CC^{\\prime}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> is a diameter of the circle. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is acute, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> must be on the opposite sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/e/d1ec033ed5c50b061a428f3a54618524c21304df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CC^{\\prime}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> (so that the circumcenter lies inside the triangle). We want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to be as close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/8719862f13b63f924f182b682c6615733f3871f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C^{\\prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> as possible to minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, but, from the first example we explored, we know that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/5/6357084247ba791f6a41713f3fee6ca53622be9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=C^{\\prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/2/df29942dbd16958ff5e6485343f28ccc1b89fe71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HM&gt;GM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />. We would reasonably expect the difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/6/016b3458cf57386e265c230685df9e1c98cf2ae3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM-HM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" /> to vary continuously as we move <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> towards <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/8719862f13b63f924f182b682c6615733f3871f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C^{\\prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" />, and this difference is positive in the second example and negative in the first example. Thus, by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Intermediate_Value_Theorem\" title=\"Intermediate Value Theorem\">Intermediate Value Theorem</a>, there should be a point on the circumcircle between these two locations for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> such that this difference is zero, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/c/d3ca3cdfb66bcba9b9499b94dae66eafa0332ee3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM=HM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" />. This point should be as close as we can get to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/1/8719862f13b63f924f182b682c6615733f3871f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C^{\\prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"16\" /> while still satisfying the inequality.\n</p><p>Now, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/c/d3ca3cdfb66bcba9b9499b94dae66eafa0332ee3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM=HM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. Further, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d31fb34078ad18b2f0e65d3ee7e485ee89effc38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD=x$\" width=\"69\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6b0b013e8a10a4ed148780fd2cdd07e83ab3fa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=9-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" />, as shown below:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98ac2a8f50c4d042080102458a715898477bb22d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  import geometry;  point A = (-5.678648, 1.454964);  point B = (-9,18); point C = (9,18); triangle t = triangle(A,B,C);  line a = altitude(t.BC); point D;  point M = midpoint(B--C);  circle c = circumcircle(t); point O = circumcenter(t);  point G = centroid(t); point H = orthocentercenter(t);  // Triangle and Circumcircle draw(t); draw(c);  // Median AM, Segment HM draw(A--M); draw(H--M);  // Altitude AD pair[] d = intersectionpoints(a,B--C); D = d[0]; draw(A--D);  // Labelling Points dot(A); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,S); dot(B); label(&quot;B&quot;,B,NW); dot(C); label(&quot;C&quot;,C,NE); dot(O); label(&quot;O&quot;,O,S); dot(M); label(&quot;M&quot;,M,N); dot(G); label(&quot;G&quot;,G,WSW); dot(H); label(&quot;H&quot;,H,ESE); dot(D); label(&quot;D&quot;,D,N);  // Length Labels label(&quot;$x$&quot;,midpoint(D--M),N); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,midpoint(M--C),N);  // Right Angle Mark markscalefactor = 0.15; draw(rightanglemark(A,D,B));  [/asy]\" width=\"248\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>By Pythagoras, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/a/4ea496451670139ea90839e327250a89a8cb3afe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM = \\sqrt{AD^2+DM^2} = \\sqrt{18^2+x^2} = \\sqrt{x^2+324}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"388\" height=\"21\" />. Thus, by centroid properties, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfa2c0e9cec77c139c9273530a5f0191957c1320.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM = \\tfrac13 AM = \\tfrac{\\sqrt{x^2+324}}3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"187\" height=\"26\" />. Now, we desire to find another expression for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/c/d3ca3cdfb66bcba9b9499b94dae66eafa0332ee3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM=HM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" />. By using Pythagoras again, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d21a8d16b81653b43e8b34d5b7e0630e7825bed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = \\sqrt{(9-x)^2+18^2} = \\sqrt{x^2-18x+405}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"341\" height=\"35\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/8179046f55dc0986356cb08dd1ac4882facd9244.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = \\sqrt{(9+x)^2+18^2} = \\sqrt{x^2+18x+405}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"340\" height=\"35\" />. Now, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ed27f8d20a85149b93307375623116c29313d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle BAC = \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" />. Also let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be0834a58059a61a79d86701cc1292ee73a0858c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=b$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/4/474cd45035e0eea00cfc2d9355528e69dc34389d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=c$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, we have the following equation:\n\\begin{align*}\nBC^2 &amp;= AB^2 + AC^2 - 2AB \\cdot AC \\cos\\alpha \\\\\n18^2 &amp;= (x^2+18x+405)+(x^2-18x+405)-2bc\\cos\\alpha \\\\\n\\frac{324}2 &amp;= x^2+405-bc\\cos\\alpha \\\\\nbc\\cos\\alpha &amp;= x^2+405-162 \\\\\n\\cos\\alpha &amp;= \\frac{x^2+243}{bc}\n\\end{align*}\nBy rearranging the formula for the area of a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc8f4f90a58046af48d7b11ee4c9cb987b62095.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{abc}{4R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"25\" height=\"24\" /> and recalling that, from the problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3f59606e18110fcc68f70d7d552254fd74d7c59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle ABC] = 162$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95e19b8cd93ed9b7412a15b81241dc4fb7759064.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R=\\tfrac{abc}{4 \\cdot 162}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"74\" height=\"24\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11ed1469a9f377b72a3ba727f83a96599f866c2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, this expression equates to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/6/cf6f22be62a834a3cc23d98ba64bb846a5fa6695.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{18bc}{4 \\cdot 162}=\\tfrac{bc}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"78\" height=\"24\" />. By the formula for the distance from a vertex to the orthocenter and substitution, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f4122856145007f73788b887b5a3f011c6ce982e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH=2R\\cos\\alpha=2(\\tfrac{bc}{36})(\\tfrac{x^2+243}{bc})=\\tfrac{x^2+243}{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"321\" height=\"26\" />. Thus, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/4/3a445b3cd8caf3a7474ad761e016b522fdf01693.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afab7771d2e9b0aea8ac807bda198206192d8e6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HD=18-\\tfrac{x^2+243}{18}=\\tfrac{81-x^2}{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"213\" height=\"26\" />. By Pythagoras in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/f/fef8e8fdff5de6a112ad93354491777be3f7625e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle HDM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/e/2de66173e777add2b88b637aa8a410f75487ac25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HM = \\sqrt{\\tfrac{(81-x^2)^2}{324}+x^2} = \\tfrac{\\sqrt{81^2-162x^2+x^4+324x^2}}{18} = \\tfrac{\\sqrt{x^4+162x^2+81^2}}{18} = \\tfrac{x^2+81}{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"543\" height=\"35\" />. Equating this with our earlier expression for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/4/5e46a5d559ffff94b22f2df24968accfa7438cbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM$\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" />, we get the following equation:\n\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{x^2+81}{18} &amp;= \\frac{\\sqrt{x^2+324}}3 \\\\\n\\frac{x^2+81}6 &amp;= \\sqrt{x^2+324} \\\\\n\\frac{x^4+162x^2+81^2}{36} &amp;= x^2+18^2 \\\\\nx^4+162x^2+81^2 &amp;= 36x^2+6^2 \\cdot 18^2 \\\\\nx^4+126x^2+81^2-108^2 &amp;= 0 \\\\\nx^4+126x^2-(108-81)(108+81) &amp;= 0 \\\\\nx^4+126x^2-27 \\cdot 189 &amp;= 0 \\\\\nx^2 &amp;= \\frac{-126 \\pm \\sqrt{126^2+4\\cdot27\\cdot189}}2 \\\\\nx^2 &amp;= -63 \\pm 36\\sqrt7\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/80336160f9dfd806f37621fd3f604771d8a85c5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/ccc358590373d8bed932e3e6fcd971f0fa384248.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2=-63+36\\sqrt7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"21\" />. Plugging this into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/c/5ecfc4de085483d4dba67740d053a74c6ac2b8d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GM=HM=\\tfrac{x^2+81}{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"162\" height=\"26\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d2ad8e6ca2fcda11a54d08825a4e09d3e3fa2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{-63+36\\sqrt7+81}{18}=\\tfrac{18+36\\sqrt7}{18}=1+2\\sqrt7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"265\" height=\"26\" />. Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cd1e3c62fc2487c3b54d42fb6c66cde49fede8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+7=\\boxed{010}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"136\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems\">2013 Mock AIME I Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">Preceded by Problem 12</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">Followed by Problem 14</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017232800\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 537/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 21640/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:28368:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017232800 and revision id 224087. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}